It is necessary to set up your .Renviorn file to enable the Shiny app to run.
You'll need to create the following private environment variables and API
keys in .Renviron:
\enumerate{
\item HACKATHON_R_SCRIPT_PATH='folder_directory_to_hackathon_r_file_scheduler.R'
(Include '/hackathon_r_file_scheduler.R' and the rest of the folder
directory in the name of the folder path. After it is generated,
'scheduler_config.rds should also be located in the folder immediately
preceding the 'hackathon_r_file_scheduler.R' file.)
\item GROQ_API_KEY='insert_your_api_key_here' (You must sign up on Groq using
your email address by going to https://console.groq.com/home and clicking on
'Continue with email' to obtain an API key from there.)
}

Additionally, since this Shiny app was tested using a shared email address,
it is recommended that you use a shared email address if you plan on testing
it yourself. Otherwise, if you are able to do so, you can change parts of the
R code so that a non-shared email address can be used instead.

There are 4 R files used to run the Shiny app. You'll need to
download and save them all to the same folder directory and make sure that
R can read from that directory for the Shiny app to run:
\enumerate{
\item app.R is where the Shiny app is run from and contains the main building
blocks for the app's UI and server logic.
\item hackathon_r_file.R uses the text from the emails to run the ad_hoc tasks
within the Shiny app based on some of the inputs made within it.
\item hackathon_r_files_scheduler is the file that runs AI summaries whenever Task Scheduler
is set up to run it. It is designed to read saved inputs from the .rds file
scheduler_config.rds every time it runs. Therefore, it is important to avoid
deleting the scheduler_config.rds file.
\item task_scheduler.R creates new tasks within the Task Scheduler software
that run hackathon_r_files_scheduler.R during given times. When the 'freq'
input is set to "DAILY", hackathon_r_files_scheduler.R will always run at the
same time each day and generate AI email summaries from emails dated within
the 24-hour time period preceding the times and days when
hackathon_r_files_scheduler.R runs. When the 'freq' input is set to "WEEKLY",
hackathon_r_files_scheduler.R will always run at the same time once during
7-day intervals and generate AI summaries from emails generated
within those intervals. When the 'freq' input is set to "MONTHLY" and the
'last_day' input tied to the Last Day of Each Month check-box is unchecked,
hackathon_r_files_scheduler.R will run at the same time and on the same day
once per month when the day input, 'start_taskscheduler_day' is set to
one value from 1 to 28. When it is set to one value from 29 to 31, it will
run on those days each month, but will not run during months that don't
contain that same day. When this file runs, it will generate AI email
summaries of emails created from the day the file runs to the same day in
the previous month.
However, checking the 'last_day' input avoids situations when the file will
not run on certain months by always running on the last day of each month.
For now, depending on if the last day of a certain month also exists as a day
in the previous month, the file will generate AI email summaries from emails
from the days that it runs to the last day of the previous month, or from the
days that it runs to the same day of the previous month.
